53e4b9bb61923780e7beef7 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; } Privacy Policy Last updated: 10 December 2025 Introduction Our commitment to protecting the privacy and the security of your personal information is as strong as our pledge to nurture and grow the products and services of tomorrow. Please read this document explaining how we use your personal information and your choices. This Privacy Notice describes how ANHEUSER-BUSCH INBEV SA/NV, a company organized and existing under the laws of Belgium, having its registered office at Grote Markt 1, 1000 Brussels, Belgium, registered with the Register of Legal Entities under company number VAT 0417.497.106 RPM Brussels, or one of our affiliated entities operating locally (“ABI”, “we”, “our” or “us”) collect, use, share, and otherwise process personal data (defined below) about visitors and users of our websites, applications, and services (the “Platform or Platforms”)” In this Privacy Notice, \"personal data\" means any information that (either in isolation or in combination with other information held by us) is related to you as an identified or identifiable individual. Please note that specific privacy notices presented in other ABI websites, applications or services shall prevail over the provisions of this Privacy Notice. This Privacy Notice is layered. If you are interested in a certain section, please open the corresponding headline. In addition to reading this Privacy Notice, we encourage you to read our Terms and Conditions, available here , which govern your access to and use of the Platform. AGE RESTRICTION: Platform is only intended for users under legal drinking age Our platforms are not directed to nor intended for users who are younger than legal drinking age, considering your local legislation. Under no circumstances may you use this Platform or submit personal information to us if you are under your local legal drinking age. False Information: If you are under of the legal drinking age and have entered this Platform by providing a false date of birth, or having someone provide false information on your behalf, you must immediately leave this Platform as you are not authorized to use. We are committed to compliance with all applicable regulations, laws, and rules, including those issued by the Beer Institute, ICAP, and COPPA. Our websites, applications and services may contain links to websites managed by third parties. This Privacy Notice does not apply to the services or products that are independently provided by third parties that are controllers of your personal information. ABI does not claim nor accept responsibility for any privacy notices, practices and/or procedures of other websites, applications or services not managed by ABI. Such independent third parties have their own policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of the personal data. If you want to learn about how they handle your personal data, we encourage you to read their privacy notice. .builder-dfe9e7fdd4a94b08a7fa8618099ec9a6 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 20px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px; } Contents: 1. What Information We Collect? 2. How We Collect Information 3. For Which Purposes Do We Use Your Information? 4. How We Share Your Information 5. How Long Do We Retain Your Personal Data For? 6. What Are Your Rights? 7. Who can you contact in case you have questions or requests? The Data Protection contact point 8. Links To Third-Party Sites 9. Security 10. Changes to this Privacy Policy and Cookie Notice .builder-3b6f3c3ee5224eeaab62147506ab81ba { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 40px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; font-family: \"Avantt-Bold\", sans-serif; pointer-events: auto; } WHAT INFORMATION WE COLLECT .builder-a174581b26b54f34b8860ec043ddbd9e { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 20px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; margin-left: 1px; } Depending on the purpose of the processing, we will process the following categories of personal data about you: Contact and transactional information. Your personal details such as name, street address, email address, online identifier (ID), username, cell phone number, date of birth and other information we may ask in connection with mailing list subscriptions, promotional offers, marketing activities or activities connected to purchases and other transactions involving you as a consumer, customer or supplier. Connection and/or browsing data. This is data that we collect by using cookies and similar tracking technologies as described under Section 8, such as device information, IP address, usage and location data. For more information see the cookies policy . Location data. We may collect and use information about the location of the device you are using only to help us identify the country where you are located and redirect you to the relevant Platform for your country. Your personal data will be processed based on your consent when you click on “Activate your geolocation” or “Allow location” tracking. Recruitment and job application information. If you apply for a job position or participate in any of our recruitment initiatives (including talent pools, internships or trainee programs), we may collect information such as your curriculum vitae (CV) or résumé, cover letter, application forms and answers to application questions; details of your professional qualifications, education and training, work history, language skills and professional memberships; information regarding your eligibility to work (such as nationality, work permit or visa status), desired role, location, salary and benefits; information collected during interviews and assessments (including test results, notes from interviews and feedback about your candidacy), as well as information provided by recruitment agencies or referees; pre‑employment screening and background check information, where permitted by applicable law and proportionate to the role; and, only where strictly necessary and permitted by applicable law, limited special categories of personal data (such as health or disability‑related information for the purpose of providing workplace adjustments, or diversity and inclusion information you choose to provide for equal opportunities monitoring). You may be able to adjust the settings of your device so that information about your physical location is no longer sent to us by (a) disabling location services within the device settings; or (b) denying certain websites or mobile applications permission to access location information by changing the relevant preferences and permissions in your mobile device or browser settings. Please note that your location may be derived from your Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and other device settings. See your device settings for more information. .builder-c1b929bd915e4cda8f26e74ef2e3c411 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; font-family: \"Avantt-Bold\", sans-serif; padding-top: 25px; } HOW WE COLLECT INFORMATION .builder-90b0c4ec2d1d46a3858001462343e7c2 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 20px; line-height: normal; height: auto; padding-left: 45px; padding-right: 50px; font-size: 20px; margin-left: 1px; font-family: \"Avantt-Regular\", sans-serif; } We collect information from different sources and across devices. For example: We collect information directly from you: When you make a purchase, register for an account or create a profile, sign up for the reward programs, sweepstakes, contests, or similar campaigns or promotions, contact us, respond to a survey, book a tour, make an appointment, RSVP for an event, interact with us on site (including in-store digital experiences), sign up to receive text messages, postage services, marketing emails, engage in transactions with us, such as the provision of products and services or other potential agreements, or apply for a job position. We may collect information from cookies or data collection technologies: We use certain standard web measurement and tracking technologies such as \"cookies,\" web server logs, web beacons (also known as \"action tags\" or \"one pixel .gif files\"), clear GIFs or other statistics programs. We do this on our Platform (including mobile apps) and in emails that we send to you. We collect information about users over time when you use this Platform. We have third parties that collect information this way, as well. To learn more about these tools and how you can control them, click here . Your browser may have an option that allows you to accept cookies, reject cookies, or receive notification when a cookie is sent, but you should note that the use of such restrictive browser settings may limit your use of the Platform. We may collect information from third parties: We process publicly available personal data in the context of due diligence procedures performed to prevent fraud, comply with legal requirements and our company policies, and protect our rights as a company. .builder-3810049942234788b7888b6916bdd460 { display: flex; flex-direction: column; position: relative; flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; margin-top: 0px; line-height: normal; height: au